## Prior-art locations

Use these as design and behavior references, not as runtime packages to copy:

- `archive/templates/` — archived authored web templates that require migration and a fresh quality pass.
- `Prototypes/ambient-mixer` — working direction for the planned Ambient Sound Mixer.
- `/Volumes/Sandisk/_archive/_backup/hitSlop.swift/_backup-templates` — legacy template catalog and metadata.
- `/Volumes/Sandisk/_archive/_backup/hitSlop.swift/Packages/SlopCore/Sources/SlopUI/SlopTemplates` — legacy SwiftUI implementations.

Every maintained template must live under `examples/slops/`, follow current
manifests and storage conventions, support direct local editing, and use
`data-slop-export="hide"` for controls that should not appear in PNG, PDF,
Quick Look, or catalog captures. A legacy implementation is reference material
until it has been migrated, reviewed, and made canonical there.
